 "title": "GRAIN | The Ellsworth Coop",
 "text": "-->\nGRAIN | The Ellsworth Coop\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nHOME\nABOUT US\nDEPARTMENTS\nAMPRIDE\nAGRONOMY\nFARM & RANCH\nGRAIN\nSERVICE STATION\nDOCUMENTS\nCONTACT US\nEMPLOYMENT\nONLINE ACCESS\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nGRAIN\nWe have 6 storage facilities, offering 3.1 million bushels of storage. Patrons are able to sell grain through our Ellsworth and Holyrood locations. We are now able to pay out your grain sales through ACH, contact the Ellsworth office if interested!\nNEWS\n7/10/2026 : Morning Grain Comments\n7/09/2026 : Morning Grain Comments\n7/08/2026 : Morning Grain Comments\n7/07/2026 : Morning Grain Comments\nSTONEX HEDGE\nYou can now market your grain through our app, powered by StoneX Hedge. After receiving an invite to join the app, follow the on-screen instructions to get your account set up.\nStoneX App Instructions\nDISCOUNT SCHEDULES\nWheat\nMilo\nCorn\nSoybeans\nSunflowers\nCONTRACTING\nDeferred\nDeferred contracts are a great option if you're needing to receive payment in the next year to offset your annual income. A deferred contract allows you to lock in a price and stop future storage charges while earning a little bit of interest on top of the sale. Deferred contracts can be rolled to the next year, please let us know by December 20th if you would like to do this. Checks are available to be picked up in either our Ellsworth or Holyrood locations or via mail on the 1st business day of the contracted payout year.\nNew Crop\nNew Crop contracts, or Future Sales and Delivery contracts, allow you to take advantage of potentially higher futures bids before your crop is in the elevator. We highly recommend contracting less than 25% of your average harvest totals to minimize risk - if you cannot fill the contracted amount, you will still be obligated to fulfill the contract by purchasing the necessary bushels through the Coop or another entity. New crop contracts can only by contracted in 1,000.00 bushel increments.\nBasis\nBasis contracts lock in the basis at the time of the contract and allows you to play out the market for a different futures bid. Cash advance options are available for up to 75% of the value of the contract. Basis contracts can only be contracted in 5,000.00 bushel increments for wheat and 1,000.00 bushel increments for row crops.\nHTA\nHTA, or Hedge to Arrive contracts, lock in a futures price and allows basis to be set at a later date. There are no fees with the original contract but fees may able if you roll a HTA to another month. HTA contracts can only be contracted in 5,000.00 bushel increments for wheat and 1,000.00 bushel increments for row crops.\nCONTACT US\nGrain\nRiley Zamrzla, Merchandiser\nrzamrzla@ellsworthcoop.com | (785) 472-3261 | (785) 531-2491\nAmy Westerman, Grain Accountant\nawesterman@ellsworthcoop.com | (785) 472-3261\nAlan Sheridan, Blackwolf Elevator Manager\n(785) 658-2697\nCole Sheridan, Kanopolis Elevator Manager\n(785) 472-4861\nNick Zajic, Holyrood Elevator Manager\n(785) 252-3233\nMain Office\n100 N Kansas Ave\nPO Box 397\nEllsworth, KS 67439\n(785) 472-3261\nHours\nMonday - Friday​\n8:00 am - 5:00pm\nbottom of page",
